From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:29:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the TWI2 and TWI7
 controllers

The SoC dtsi describes only the two R_TWI controllers. Boards that bring
TWI2 or TWI7 out on a pin header cannot use them.

Add TWI2 at 0x02512000 and TWI7 at 0x02517000, with their bus clocks and
resets. They have the register set of the R_TWI controllers, so they use
the same compatible chain and the mv64xxx driver binds. The TWI controllers
have no module clock of their own. Add the pin groups that reach the
Cubie A7S header: TWI2 on PD16/PD17 and TWI7 on PJ22/PJ23, both function 6.
Both nodes are disabled; a board enables them.

PD16/PD17 and PJ22/PJ23 can also carry UART3, so a board uses either the
TWI or the UART function on a pin pair.

Not covered: DMA requests and the packet engine at offset 0x200, which the
driver does not use; the other TWI controllers.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with both nodes enabled in a copy of the DTB,
both controllers probe, take PD16/PD17 and PJ22/PJ23, and scan the empty
header buses without an error.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 6a5e8a74d7b0..599e9a00e2d8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -494,6 +494,20 @@ i2c0_pg_pins: i2c0-pg-pins {
 				function = "i2c0";
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			i2c2_pd_pins: i2c2-pd-pins {
+				pins = "PD16", "PD17";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "i2c2";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			i2c7_pj_pins: i2c7-pj-pins {
+				pins = "PJ22", "PJ23";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "i2c7";
+			};
+
 			/omit-if-no-ref/
 			i2s0_pb_pins: i2s0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB4", "PB5", "PB6", "PB7", "PB8";
@@ -688,6 +702,32 @@ i2c0: i2c@2510000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		i2c2: i2c@2512000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c";
+			reg = <0x02512000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 13 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_I2C2>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_I2C2>;
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
+		i2c7: i2c@2517000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c";
+			reg = <0x02517000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 18 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_I2C7>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_I2C7>;
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
 		gpadc: adc@2521000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-gpadc",
 				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc";
